# Which One Should You Learn First?

For production RAG, learn in this order:

```text
1. Dense Search
2. BM25
3. Hybrid Search
4. RRF
5. MMR
6. Cross Encoder Reranker
7. Context Compression
```

And if you look at modern systems such as [Elasticsearch](https://www.elastic.co?utm_source=chatgpt.com), [OpenSearch](https://opensearch.org?utm_source=chatgpt.com), [Weaviate](https://weaviate.io?utm_source=chatgpt.com), and [Qdrant](https://qdrant.tech?utm_source=chatgpt.com), you'll find that **RRF has become the default fusion strategy in many hybrid-search deployments** because it works surprisingly well without requiring score calibration.
